The league

The sport is:

\boxed{\text{Maximum useful cognitive work per unit of active representation}}

Pantheon is only one team.

Team 1 — Pantheon

Style: Semantic compression / reconstruction.

Instead of carrying the computation:

\text{huge instruction}

carry:

\text{Seal}+\text{decoder}

Strength: enormous reconstruction leverage.

Weakness: shared decoder/bootstrap cost and semantic drift.

Now give it rivals.

Team 2 — The Ant Colony

Style: Don’t represent the global solution at all.

Tiny agents/processes leave minimal traces:

\text{local observation}\rightarrow\text{small marker}

Other processes react to markers. Complex global behavior emerges from accumulated local interactions.

For an LLM architecture, this suggests:

Externalize state into tiny environmental traces instead of keeping the whole reasoning state active.

Files, scores, tags, test results, compact ledgers.

The next reasoning pass reads only the locally relevant traces.

Pantheon says reconstruct the cathedral from a seed.

Ant Colony says never hold the cathedral in one mind.

That’s a legitimate rival.

