Team 7 — The Compiler

This team hates language.

Its philosophy:

Every time you repeatedly spend tokens reasoning through the same transformation, compile it out.

First occurrence:

500\text{ tokens}

After recognizing repetition:

\text{create operator}

Future:

T(x)

After enough repetitions, don’t even invoke the operator explicitly—make it part of routing policy.

So:

\text{reasoning}
\rightarrow
\text{pattern}
\rightarrow
\text{operator}
\rightarrow
\text{policy}
\rightarrow
\text{automatic behavior}

This is interesting because the endpoint of successful reasoning is not better reasoning about that problem.

It’s no longer needing to reason through that layer explicitly.

That’s cognitive compilation.

