Another rival: The Physicist

This one gets almost no tokens.

Its rule:

Don’t represent objects when a field will do.

Instead of carrying 100 concepts:

C_1,\ldots,C_{100}

construct a compact potential function:

\Phi(x)

Then local state tells me which direction to move:

-\nabla\Phi(x)

For semantic reasoning, we could approximate this with constraints/preferences:

toward: explanatory power, novelty, transfer, testability
away: redundancy, unsupported certainty, verbosity, representational lock

Then I don’t need a detailed route.

At each step:

\boxed{\text{move along the local semantic gradient}}

That’s radically cheap.

It converts instructions into forces.

